[thin] These two 0.493 mm measurements lie along the fixed stops' X +/-18 end planes into the curved side-wall boundary at the Y6 fore cut. Exact CAD traces inward from each stop end for 3.750 mm, from the curved face for 3.000 mm, and from the fore cut for more than 27 mm of connected stock. These are finite end-plane/curve junctions, not thin stationary fins or model-to-model release gaps.
alternatives: Extending each stop outboard covers this end-plane junction with additional stop stock beyond the motion stop plane. A 4 mm shell adds material and narrows the cavity; enlarging the outside to preserve that cavity increases the reference object's size. Filling the curved boundary with square stock removes part of the retained curve from view.
