[thin] The 1.080 mm minimum is at the lower end of the flute backing beside the stop's upper corner. Exact CAD supplies 4.200 mm inward through the backing and 3.750 mm through the stop's end plane, with 20 mm of connected stock along the pad. The ranking gathers the surrounding ordinary 3 mm skins into the same place; its minimum diagonal does not describe those skins' normal thickness.
alternatives: Extending the stop outward covers the corner with stock outside its working plane. Continuing the backing to the bed removes its lower end but adds material below the texture field. A 4.2 mm full flank adds stock outside that field and reduces cavity access.
