[thin] These curved-skin rankings read the analytic 3 mm inward offset of the R6 envelope. Exact CAD normal traces at all six anchors supply 3.000 mm; the printed mesh reads 2.998..2.999 mm across its chords. The additive tangent fill increases stock outside the retained offset. These readings establish local geometry, not load capacity or surface acceptance.
alternatives: A 4 mm shell adds material across the compact body and reduces the interior cavity. Enlarging the outside envelope to preserve the cavity increases the reference object's size. More printed walls changes the recipe, not the analytic offset.
