[thin] The two 3.000 mm readings run through the fixed capture-lip stock from Z7.40 to Z10.40. The lips are joined to their guide walls and geometrically retain the moving shoulders through the 10 mm stroke. Their 0.48 mm lower release air is a functional void and does not reduce the lip's own 3 mm stock; release and retention remain physically unmeasured.
alternatives: A 4 mm lip adds material above the same release surface. Thickening downward consumes the release air. Increasing overlap into the handle space narrows that space and changes the fit being observed.
