[ledge] The 4.25 square millimetre face is the exposed lower edge of the local flute backing beside the stop, at Z6. The adjacent ordinary wall and connected backing retain their full normal stock; its small 0.25 mm exposed width is not a thin wall. Automatic support choices remain permitted here, with cleanup through the open rear and unused travel spaces; removal effort is unmeasured.
alternatives: Extending the stop to X18.25 covers the ledge with additional outboard stock. Continuing the backing to the bed adds material outside the flute field. A sloped inner transition adds a further wall shape and changes local support deposition without adding a selected reading.
